        "original_id": "0901946b-2355-5e94-9c19-03afed5a5370",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wilfrid Brambell, Harry H. Corbett, Paul McCartney, Ray Galton, Alan Simpson\n- Works: Steptoe and Son Ride Again, A Hard Day's Night, Some Will, Some Won't, Get Well Soon, Steptoe and Son\n- Concepts: fictional grandfather, cameo performance, tuberculosis sanatorium\n\nFacts:\n- In 1947, Ray Galton and Alan Simpson met in a tuberculosis sanatorium, and Get Well Soon was based on that meeting.\n- Wilfrid Brambell performed alongside the Beatles in A Hard Day's Night, playing Paul McCartney's fictional grandfather.\n- Steptoe and Son Ride Again again starred Wilfrid Brambell and Harry H. Corbett.\n- Some Will, Some Won't featured a cameo performance by Steptoe and Son actor Wilfrid Brambell as Henry Russell.\n- In Some Will, Some Won't, Henry Russell leaves four family members £150,000 in his will on the condition that they complete bizarre tasks he set for them.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
